    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "WAF rule present",
      "description": "Result of the managed zone custom rule (ref abuseipdb) step at the last push that reached it. Pushes run every 6h, and a failure in the list stage skips this step and keeps the previous value. Present (1): the rule was confirmed, and created, re-enabled or corrected if needed; a rule deleted in the Cloudflare dashboard afterwards still shows Present until the next push. Not confirmed (0): the check or repair failed (API, permission, rate-limit or network error; the rule may still exist); see Cloudflare sync errors by reason. Exporter 0.3.1 also reports 0 when the push failed before reaching the rule step. Unknown: no push has reached the rule step since the synchronizer started (exporter 0.3.1 exports 0 until then; the tile hides that 0 once nothing failed).",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
