    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Detailed source-IP investigation",
      "description": "Per-IP investigation is intentionally not exposed as Prometheus labels. Use Loki for synchronizer logs and Hubble for Cilium flow decisions.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 40,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Where enforcement happens**\n\n- **Cloudflare edge (real client IPs):** account IP list `abuseipdb` referenced by the zone WAF custom rule `ip.src in $abuseipdb` (action Block). This is what protects the proxied public hostnames.\n- **Cilium (direct paths):** `CiliumCIDRGroup/abuseipdb` + `CiliumClusterwideNetworkPolicy deny-abuseipdb-ingress` on `reserved:ingress`, for direct-to-origin/LAN traffic. Cilium only sees Cloudflare edge addresses for proxied traffic.\n\n**Synchronizer logs (Loki)**\n\n```logql\n{namespace=\"abuseipdb\"} | json\n{namespace=\"abuseipdb\"} |= \"Cloudflare edge sink updated\"\n{namespace=\"abuseipdb\"} |= \"synchronization failed\"\n```\n\n**Cilium flow detail (Hubble CLI, per source IP)**\n\n```shell\nhubble observe --verdict DROPPED --last 100\nhubble observe --from-ip <suspected-source-ip>\n```\n\nFor per-IP block detail (Cloudflare edge blocks and Cilium Gateway drops), open the **Blocked Sources** dashboard."
      }
    }
